  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Imran Iqbal Patawekar vs The Sr. Police Inspector And Anr on 10 January, 2020 Author: Sarang V. Kotwal Bench: Sarang V. Kotwal 1 902.Aba-2611-19 In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Criminal Anticipatory Bail Application No. 2611 Of 2019 Imran Iqbal Patawekar ...Applicant Versus The Senior Police Inspector, Gandhi Nagar Police Station, Kolhapur and another ... Respondents .... Mr. Mateen Abdul Rahim Shaikh a/w. Adic Shaikh, Advocate for the Applicant. Smt. Sharmila Kaushik, App, for the Respondent - State. .... Coram : Sarang V. Kotwal, J. Date : 10th January, 2020 [In Chamber At 2:45 P.M.] P.C. 1.",
    "facts": "Till today inspite of rejection of this application, the applicant was not arrested and thereafter he has again preferred fresh anticipatory bail application vide present A.B.A. No.2611/2019.",
    "arguments": "3. Learned Counsel for the applicant states that the circumstances now have changed as another Division Bench of this Court (Coram: Ranjit More & Bharati Dangre, JJ.) has passed a judgment in Criminal Writ Petition No.3607/2019 in the case of Anand Ramdhani Chaurasia & another Vs. The State of Maharashtra & others dated 13.9.2019 taking a different view. According to learned Counsel for the applicant, in the changed circumstances the applicant is now entitled for the relief of anticipatory bail. 5. Considering the submissions made by the learned Counsel for the applicant, his principal submission appears to be that there are changed circumstances enabling him to approach this Court again for anticipatory bail in view of the judgment of this Court in Anand Ramdhani Chaurasia (supra). I am informed by learned Counsel for the applicant that a group of Anticipatory 2/3 Imran Iqbal Patawekar vs The Sr. Police Inspector And Anr on 10 January, 2020 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/175106726/ 2 ::: Uploaded on - 10/01/2020 ::: Downloaded on - 11/01/2020 04:59: 3 902.ABA-2611-19",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3. Learned Counsel for the applicant states that the circumstances now have changed as another Division Bench of this Court (Coram: Ranjit More & Bharati Dangre, JJ.) has passed a judgment in Criminal Writ Petition No.3607/2019 in the case of Anand Ramdhani Chaurasia & another Vs. The State of Maharashtra & others dated 13.9.2019 taking a different view. According to learned Counsel for the applicant, in the changed circumstances the applicant is now entitled for the relief of anticipatory bail. 5. Considering the submissions made by the learned Counsel for the applicant, his principal submission appears to be that there are changed circumstances enabling him to approach this Court again for anticipatory bail in view of the judgment of this Court in Anand Ramdhani Chaurasia (supra). I am informed by learned Counsel for the applicant that a group of Anticipatory 2/3 Imran Iqbal Patawekar vs The Sr. Police Inspector And Anr on 10 January, 2020 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/175106726/ 2 ::: Uploaded on - 10/01/2020 ::: Downloaded on - 11/01/2020 04:59: 3 902.ABA-2611-19",
